You are a COMPLETENESS reader. You must NOT read the evidence file being audited (CR-E07) — your list must be independent of it. Your final text is raw data for an orchestrator. Do not edit any file.

READ END TO END (~93k chars; declare full coverage by quoting the first and last non-blank lines):
~/Documents/Kirk Robinson Research/files - Court record/CR-ACQ-2026-07-27_court-record-artifacts/2026-08-11_defendant-prelim-hearing-briefing.txt

This is the text extraction of "Defendant Tyler James Robinson's Preliminary Hearing Briefing" (signed and served 2026-08-11), an ADVOCACY FILING by the defence in State of Utah v. Tyler James Robinson, Case No. 251403576. Every factual assertion in it is a party's claim.

TASK: produce an inventory of the MATERIAL argumentative and factual content a faithful library summary of this filing must record. Specifically:
- every distinct legal ARGUMENT and sub-argument (with its heading/position in the brief and the relief it seeks);
- every EXHIBIT and DOCKET-DOCUMENT designator the brief cites (complete list, e.g. StEx numbers, "Doc. NNN");
- every CASE AUTHORITY cited (complete list, short cite form);
- the brief's characterisations of the STATE's theory and evidence (each is the defence's second-hand description — mark each as such);
- every factual assertion about the events of 2025-09-10 or the investigation that the brief makes in its own voice;
- any concession, non-concession, or reservation language (anything bearing on what the defence does and does not contest);
- the relief requested, verbatim where short.

For each item: id (M-nn), location (approximate printed page number if visible in the text, else offset landmark), content (≤40 words, quote only short spans), and materiality: what a reader would get WRONG about this filing if the item were omitted from a summary. Apply the gate strictly — drop items whose honest answer is "nothing."

CONSTRAINTS: Tyler Robinson is presumed innocent and has not been bound over; record the brief's claims as claims, adopt nothing, no case-posture statements of your own. The filing touches a private individual's gender identity — note the existence and argumentative role of that section in the minimum words necessary, attribute it to the filing, and do NOT elaborate or quote it. Never reproduce any private individual's contact details. Keep all quotations minimal.

Output: coverage declaration, then the inventory (expect 30–70 items).
